# RayWaves game project

C++23 gameplay compiled to `@GAMELOGIC_MODULE@`. Levels are `rw::Level` subclasses in
`@SOURCE_DIR@/`. Scenes are INI files in `@ASSET_DIR@/<MapId>.scene`.

## Before editing

1. Read `AGENTS.md` in the project root.
2. Run `rwcli doctor . --json`.
3. Run `rwcli build . --json` to confirm the baseline compiles.

## Tooling

`rwcli` lives in the RayWaves package, not in this folder. Use the generated
wrapper from the project root:

```text
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ doctor . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ info . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ maps . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ build . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ run . --frames 120 --screenshot shot.png --state state.json --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ run . --frames 120 --input input.txt --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ scene list . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ lsp . --check --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ validate . --json
```

The wrapper is `.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd` on Windows and `.raywaves/bin/rwcli` on Linux.
If the wrapper is missing or stale, read `.raywaves/tooling.ini` and use
`[rwcli] path`. If `available=0`, `rwcli` was not packaged; build the `rwcli`
target or ask the user. Full flags, JSON and exit codes:
`.agents/skills/raywaves-game/reference.md`.

Quote paths with spaces. Suppress informational stderr with `2>$null` on
PowerShell or `2>/dev/null` on bash. Headless Linux runs need
`xvfb-run -a` (and `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1` without a GPU driver).

## Loop

1. Edit `@SOURCE_DIR@/*.cpp` or `*.h`.
2. `rwcli build . --json`; fix `diagnostics[]` and rebuild.
3. `rwcli run ... --json`; check `screenshot.nonEmpty`, `entities[]`, `state`.
4. For movement or interaction, add `--input` events and assert entity positions.

## API

```cpp
#include "rw.h"

class MyLevel : public rw::Level
{
public:
    MyLevel() : rw::Level("MyLevel") {}

protected:
    void OnStart() override
    {
        m_Texture.Load("player.png");
        m_Player = Spawn("Player", { 320, 240 }, { 48, 64 }, rw::Origin::Center);
        Cam().SetZoom(1.0f);
    }

    void OnUpdate(float dt) override
    {
        if (rw::IsKeyDown(KEY_RIGHT)) { m_Player->position.x += 240.0f * dt; }
        Cam().Follow(m_Player->position, dt);
    }

    void OnDraw() override { rw::DrawSprite(m_Texture, *m_Player); }

private:
    rw::Texture m_Texture;
    rw::Entity* m_Player = nullptr;
};

RW_GAME(MyLevel)
```

- `rw::Game` + `AddLevel<T>("id")` for multiple levels.
- `rwcli new-level . MyLevel` scaffolds a level and registers it.
- `Spawn` registers the entity with the editor and `rwcli` state.
- `OnSceneLoaded()` + `SceneObjectsOfType("spawn")` read editor markers.
- `entity->Expose("Speed", &m_Speed, 0.0f, 500.0f)` adds an Inspector field.
- Use `rw::IsKeyDown` / `rw::IsKeyPressed` / `rw::IsMouseButtonDown` so
  `--input` can drive the game.
- Assets resolve through `@ASSET_DIR@/`.

## Input script

```text
# frame,key,down|up
0,KEY_RIGHT,down
30,KEY_RIGHT,up
0,mouse,640,360
```

## Rules

- Gameplay only in `@SOURCE_DIR@/`. No gameplay in the engine.
- `RW_GAME(...)` exactly once.
- Never edit `.raywaves/`; it is generated.
- Do not hand-edit `compile_commands.json`, `.clangd`, or `.vscode/`; run
  `rwcli lsp . --force` after moving the project or updating the engine.
- Asset names: `A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -`.

## Error codes

- `build_failed`: read `diagnostics[]` (`file`, `line`, `column`).
- `build_locked`: another process owns `.raywaves/agent.lock`.
- `dll_missing`: run `rwcli build`.
- `dll_load` / `abi_mismatch`: rebuild GameLogic against this engine.
- `run_crashed`: see `logs`; the game process died.
- `run_timeout`: raise `--timeout` or lower `--frames`.
- `input_missing`: pass an existing `--input` file.

## Editor

Open the folder in VS Code. `.clangd` and `.vscode/` are generated. Re-run
`rwcli lsp` if the engine path changes. `compile_commands.json` is generated by
`rwcli lsp` and is gitignored.
